msgid ""
"Make machines reachable at the IP layer over QUIC datagrams.\n"
"\n"
"Creates a TUN interface (needs root / CAP_NET_ADMIN on Linux and macOS, or Administrator + wintun.dll on Windows). `tun serve` is the coordination hub (roster + fallback forward); `tun connect` dials it, learns the VIP↔EndpointId roster, and tries direct spoke↔spoke links (hub forward remains the fallback). Prefer `--cc bbr3` on lossy paths. Virtual IPs are IPv4 only — see docs/subsystems/tun.md."
msgstr ""
"Haz que las máquinas se alcancen en capa IP con datagramas QUIC.\n"
"\n"
"Crea un TUN (root/CAP_NET_ADMIN en Linux/macOS, o Administrador + wintun.dll en Windows). `tun serve` es el hub de coordinación (roster + reenvío de respaldo); `tun connect` marca, aprende el roster VIP↔EndpointId e intenta enlaces directos (el hub queda de respaldo). Prefiere `--cc bbr3` en rutas con pérdida. Las IP virtuales son solo IPv4 — ver docs/subsystems/tun.md."

msgid ""
"Hub: accept many concurrent peers, broadcast the VIP↔EndpointId roster, bridge this machine to each at the IP layer, and forward traffic when spokes have no direct path. Prints this node's virtual IP and EndpointId."
msgstr ""
"Hub: acepta muchos peers concurrentes, difunde el roster VIP↔EndpointId, puentea esta máquina en capa IP y reenvía cuando no hay ruta directa. Imprime la IP virtual y el EndpointId."

msgid ""
"Dial a `tun serve` hub, install 172.24.0.0/16 on the TUN, receive the mesh roster, and attempt direct links to other spokes (packets prefer direct; otherwise via hub)."
msgstr ""
"Marca un hub `tun serve`, instala 172.24.0.0/16 en el TUN, recibe el roster e intenta enlaces directos (preferencia directa; si no, vía hub)."

